# Marketing stays local, never in the repo (repo may go public later)
/Marketing/

# DF26 framework - owned by the DataFlex package manager (per-DF-major content).
# Untracked 2026-08-20 so df-cli/Studio 26 can own these without deleting tracked files.
/DfPkg/
AppHtml/WebUI/
AppHtml/CSSThemes/

# DFUnit's package drops its scaffold launcher into the consuming workspace's root
# (package.install in RDC-DFUnit-Library.sws). Same class as the entries above: written by the
# package manager on install, not ours to track. Root-anchored so it cannot shadow a
# same-named file elsewhere in the tree.
/SetupUnitTests.bat
/SetupUnitTests.ps1
# DUF's package drops its build script the same way (package.install in RDC-DUF-Library.sws):
# BuildDUFUtilities.bat compiles DUF's utility programs in this workspace. Written by the
# package manager on install, not ours to track.
/BuildDUFUtilities.bat

# Library-RDCFlexTron's package installs its five style sheets here (package.install in
# RDC-FlexTron-Library.sws) - written by the package manager, not ours to track.
AppHtml/RDCFlexTron/
# ... and into Bitmaps: RDCFlexTron's dark toolbar and menu icons (Bitmaps\RDCFlexTron\Dk)
Bitmaps/RDCFlexTron/

# Generated / local debris - none of these has ever been tracked (verified 2026-08-20).
# The Z* trees under Data were WRITTEN BY THE TESTS (oLibraryInventory-Tests /
# oWorkspaceCopyPlan-Tests) until 2026-10-05; the tests build them in the Windows temp folder
# now. The two rules stay for a test runner built before that, which still writes them here.
/Data/ZCopyPlanTest/
/Data/ZLibInvTest/
/Data/ModAnalyzerRecipes.json
/Data/ScopeIndex-*.json
*.dbg
*.stackdump
*.sws.lock
# EXPORT-DIALOG ARTIFACTS - never commit these. Program Settings -> Export to ini-file writes
# <name>.ini plus a _RUN.ps1 wrapper and a _RESULT.txt beside it, all naming the WORKSPACE it was
# exported for. They carry a customer name, that customer's folder layout and the local user name,
# and this repo's origin is public. Was one line per customer (Order_Entry, then CMOS); a pattern
# so the next export is covered before anyone has to notice it.
/Programs/DFRefactor_*.ini
/Programs/DFRefactor_*_RUN.ps1
/Programs/DFRefactor_*_SCAN.ps1
/Programs/DFRefactor_*_SCAN-RESULT.txt
/Programs/DFRefactor_*_CI-SAMPLE.yml
/Programs/DFRefactor_*_RESULT.txt
# ...and what /scan writes beside such an INI (2026-11-20): its findings, their SARIF and the baseline name the
# same workspace and its files.
/Programs/DFRefactor_*.findings.json
/Programs/DFRefactor_*.findings.sarif
/Programs/DFRefactor_*.baseline.json
/Programs/ScintillaEditOLD.ini

# MetaTagCheck service-program output - regenerated on every run
MetaTagCheck.log.txt

# FunctionHelpGen service-program output - regenerated on every run
FunctionHelp/

# HELP BUILD OUTPUT. The .chm IS tracked - it is a runtime dependency (psHelpFile in DFRefactor,
# DFRefactorFT and TestBench), so a clone without it has a broken F1. These two are not:
#   .chw - not HelpNDoc output at all. hh.exe writes it on the READER's machine as a search-index
#          cache, so it is machine-local and it dirties the tree just by opening the help.
#   .pdf - nothing references it, the same content is browsable at the GitHub Pages site, and it
#          is ~900 KB per regenerate against 20.5 MB of Help/ blobs already in history. Attach it
#          to a release when shipping; the .hnd outside this repo is the source of truth.
*.chw
/Help/DFRefactor.pdf

# Python bytecode from Tools/ scripts
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# MAINTAINER NOTES AND SCRATCH, not part of the product. User-facing documentation is Help/
# (the .chm is a runtime dependency - psHelpFile - plus the tour and About). What collected in
# Documents/ was correspondence and working notes: two letters to the Win32 projection author,
# a library-publishing checklist, and loose scratch. None of it helps anyone USING DFRefactor,
# and the one measurement in it that could not be re-derived now lives in the header of
# cWin32ProjectionHarvester.pkg - which declares that it stands alone, and is where a maintainer
# actually looks. Untracked 2026-08-30, files left on disk; keep using the folder for scratch.
Documents/
